Dear Patient,
The pain is probably due to a rib fracture. The fracture is most likely to be in the upper portion of the rib cage.
If you are experiencing pain in your ribs it is important that you seek immediate care. If the pain persists for more than a day or two, then you should consult a doctor. You should also tell your doctor if you have a history of broken ribs, or if your rib is displaced. Pain in bones is always something to get a physician's attention, since it can be a sign of a much more serious condition. Good luck!
