I agree with you that your symptoms could be a result of a high/low blood sugar or heart condition. However, it is wise to see your doctor before you make a rash decision to take a blood thinner or cholesterol lowering drug. In most cases, these drugs are over prescribed and can cause a whole host of other issues. See your primary care doctor and get his/her opinion. When you see the doctor, have them do a chest X-ray. This will show the extent of your coronary artery disease and if there are any other signs of an artery problem. Also, there is a good chance that you will need to go on a cholesterol/heart attack diet. These diets are usually very restrictive and your body will start to burn its own fat instead of using it for energy. They work well for some people, however, they are not a quick fix. Make sure to eat a healthy diet and stay active. Take care. Please let me know how you get on. Best of luck.}}
